-- ============================================================================
-- DR2 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Torque, Drag & Casing Wear, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, so the seeded structure and the
-- shipped lesson files cannot disagree.
--
-- What this tier owns: the soft-string model and the hookload. A drill string
-- as a heavy cable with no bending stiffness; torque and drag as two
-- components of ONE friction force resolved in two directions; buoyancy as a
-- single factor because the string is in one fluid; side force from exactly
-- two sources, tension times curvature and the weight component perpendicular
-- to an inclined hole, BOTH of which vanish in a vertical well; the recursion
-- marching UP from the bit because that is where the boundary condition is;
-- one pair of direction cosines producing every difference between the six
-- operations; pick up, rotate and slack off and the three different
-- differences people call drag; and the horizontal well whose slack-off
-- hookload is NEGATIVE, which is the model telling you it has left its own
-- domain.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored
-- engines/drilling against its own goldens, and the teaching lab that the
-- panels and this course share is pinned to the same values by
-- torquedragLab.test.js. A numeric sweep over the lessons resolved all 403
-- literals carrying seven or more significant figures to an engine-derived
-- value; a tier-leakage sweep over the lessons and the banks reports zero
-- downward leaks and zero same-tier answer prints against all eighteen graded
-- fields.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

values ('torquedrag', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-torque-and-drag-is","title":"What Torque and Drag Is","lesson_keys":["l01-a-rope-that-can-push-a-little","l02-the-string-this-course-runs","l03-buoyancy-and-the-weight-you-lift","l04-what-the-answer-is-for"]},{"key":"m02-the-soft-string-model","title":"The Soft-String Model","lesson_keys":["l01-side-force-from-tension-and-curvature","l02-the-two-sources-of-side-force","l03-marching-up-from-the-bit","l04-what-soft-string-leaves-out","l05-the-step-and-what-it-costs"]},{"key":"m03-hookload","title":"Hookload","lesson_keys":["l01-pick-up-rotate-and-slack-off","l02-the-vertical-well-has-no-drag","l03-drag-is-a-difference","l04-the-broomstick-plot","l05-the-hookload-that-went-negative"]},{"key":"m04-the-operations","title":"The Operations","lesson_keys":["l01-six-operations-one-string","l02-tripping","l03-rotating-on-and-off-bottom","l04-sliding","l05-back-reaming"]},{"key":"m05-reading-the-output","title":"Reading the Output","lesson_keys":["l01-tension-along-the-string","l02-the-neutral-point","l03-warnings-and-what-they-mean","l04-checking-against-a-closed-form"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
